; hbnf config grammar, as an ASTBNF schema over the parsed node tree.
;
; Built-in core types (interpreted by the codegen, never part of the grammar):
;   str   = a quoted c-string (carries its own "string" designation)
;   atom  = a bare token with no whitespace: a symbol or a number.  The
;           matcher narrows it against the typed cores below with full type
;           checking.  `word` is a synonym for `atom`.
;   int / dec / float / bool / flag / u8..u64 / i8..i64 = typed atoms.
;
; hbnf AST nodes map to these rules: Directive -> statement, Block -> block;
; Comment nodes are carried, not matched.  Value kinds: Word -> atom,
; Str -> str, Int -> int, Dec -> dec.  A statement ends with ";" or "\n";
; both are match-and-skip terminals (string literals, decoded by astbnf).

config    = *entry
entry     = statement / block
statement = name *arg (";" / "\n")
block     = name [qualifier] "{" *entry "}"
name      = atom
qualifier = str / atom
arg       = atom / str / int / dec
